// SignedOrderV2 is the upstream-locked signed order envelope.
// signature_scheme accepts exactly lowercase "eip712" and is not persisted on
// Task state. user_signature is recoverable 65-byte R||S||V with V in {27,28}
// and low-S. It signs the "TrueOpen Task Order" version "3" EIP-712 digest,
// whose feeDenom is hub.v1 Params phase0.business_denom (see TaskOrderV3), and
// whose domain chainId is signature_chain_id.
// Recover once: the owner address selects wallet verification against the
// stored account public key; otherwise require the current session key. The
// owner must match StreamState.owner_user_address and have a stored public key
// on both paths. Delegated first admission additionally requires an ACTIVE/IDLE
// session, current_height <= session_key_expiry_height, a canonical signed
// session_anchor_height >= session_key_set_height, and checked spent + max_fee
// <= spend_cap when the cap is nonzero (zero means unlimited). All other
// admission rules remain in force. Increment spent with checked addition only
// on first delegated admission, atomically with sequence consumption and escrow.
// Later proposals, settlement, refunds and genesis validation of admitted tasks
// do not reauthorize against the current grant or count max_fee again.
// Session key failures propagate as ERR_SESSION_KEY_INVALID,
// ERR_SESSION_KEY_EXPIRED or ERR_SESSION_KEY_SPEND_CAP_EXCEEDED, not a generic
// assignment error. No signer-kind field or new signing domain is introduced.
//
// signature_chain_id is chosen by the signer: a browser wallet uses its active
// network, so the user never switches networks. It must be in 1..MaxInt64;
// 0 is rejected as malformed. The verifier rebuilds the domain from it and the
// signature covers it. Cross-chain isolation comes only from the chainId string
// (TaskOrderV3.chain_id), which the verifier takes from its own chain.
// signature_scheme, user_signature and signature_chain_id are signature
// metadata: they enter neither task_hash, task_id nor any opening, and no
// identity, replay, dedup or exact-retry binding may include them. The same
// order signed under another signature_chain_id is the same order.
